Part 9. Arithmetic
  Proposition 3.6(a) with d = ceil(sqrt n) tests gives at least (sqrt 2 - 1) sqrt n, for n = 1, ..., 200000: True
  floor(n/2) >= 0.5 sqrt(n) ln n for n = 1, ..., 3000000: violations 0
  K(B) + 2 for pi(B) = 1/(2n): log2(2n) + 2 = log2(n) + 3, e.g. n = 10^6: 22.932 = 22.932
  if the halving potential doubled at every non-zero increment the bound would be K + 1; it is 1, 1, 2, 4, ..., which gives K + 2
  2 ln 2 = 1.38629 <= 1.39;  e/(e-1) = 1.58198 < 1.582

all parts finished
